    {
      "id": "p0159-b003",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "In the English script, a character called \"Monster Kid\" speaks like an energetic youth who loves to use slang. The translator preserved these attributes in Japanese, but this led to a problem: Monster Kid's gender is never specified in the original script, yet this Japanese speaking style makes the character sound like a teenage boy. After consulting with Toby, the translator gave Monster Kid the assertive, masculine pronoun ore.",
        "raw": "In the English script, a character called \"Monster Kid\" speaks like an energetic\nyouth who loves to use slang. The translator preserved these attributes in\nJapanese, but this led to a problem: Monster Kid's gender is never specified in\nthe original script, yet this Japanese speaking style makes the character sound\nlike a teenage boy. After consulting with Toby, the translator gave Monster Kid\nthe assertive, masculine pronoun ore.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.08767842,
          0.26222143,
          0.69644637,
          0.36685714
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.08563702,
          0.26150714,
          0.69848777,
          0.36792857
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          20,
          23,
          25,
          28,
          29,
          30
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "英文剧本中，Monster Kid 像个精力旺盛、爱说俚语的孩子。译者在日语里保留了这些特征，却遇到了问题：原文从未说明 Monster Kid 的性别，但这种日语说话风格，会让角色听起来像个少年。征询 Toby 后，译者为 Monster Kid 选用了态度鲜明、偏男性的第一人称 ore（我）。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": [
          {
            "start": 142,
            "end": 145,
            "italic": true,
            "lang": "en"
          }
        ]
      },
