    {
      "id": "p0159-b004",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "In early drafts of the Japanese script, Monster Kid's laughter was denoted by the letter \"w\", which is the Japanese equivalent of \"LOL\" (laughing out loud) in English. Eventually, the localization team agreed that \"w\" felt too out of place, and gave the character a normal laugh instead.",
        "raw": "In early drafts of the Japanese script, Monster Kid's laughter was denoted by\nthe letter \"w\", which is the Japanese equivalent of \"LOL\" (laughing out loud)\nin English. Eventually, the localization team agreed that \"w\" felt too out of\nplace, and gave the character a normal laugh instead.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.08907679,
          0.38237143,
          0.68345281,
          0.44920714
