    {
      "id": "p0159-b010",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "Toby noted that this is reference to the famous quote from Shakespeare's Macbeth, \"Out, damned spot! Out, I say!\". Naturally, the translator consulted a Japanese translation of Macbeth and adapted the equivalent quote for Woshua's battle text. Although the reference is less recognizable in Japanese, the line fortunately still fits Woshua's dirt despising personality.",
        "raw": "Toby noted that this is reference to\nthe famous quote from Shakespeare's\nMacbeth, \"Out, damned spot! Out,\nI say!\". Naturally, the translator\nconsulted a Japanese translation\nof Macbeth and adapted the\nequivalent quote for Woshua's battle\ntext. Although the reference is less\nrecognizable in Japanese, the line\nfortunately still fits Woshua's dirt\ndespising personality.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.08857664,
          0.70366429,
          0.37733365,
          0.90112857
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.08563702,
